\paragraph{\cwm{} convergence analysis.}
\label{app:cwm_convergence}
Qwen3-8B \cwm{} repo-level eval loss reaches its minimum within ${\sim}$5\% of training (step 300--400 of 6{,}633) and increases monotonically thereafter, with no plateau or recovery (Table~\ref{tab:cwm_convergence}). This pattern is consistent across all three seeds, confirming systematic overfitting to trace generation rather than stochastic variation. The final-epoch eval loss is ${\sim}$1.8$\times$ the optimal value. By contrast, function-level \cwm{} achieves \cls{}-equivalent accuracy (TOST $p{=}0.007$) with the same training recipe, indicating that the overfit is specific to repo-level output complexity.

